  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ecological Restoration Of Mangroves In N</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will restore and conserve 714 acres of mangrove and coastal areas. Additionally, it will focus on strengthening local capacity for conservation in the region and cultivate relationships with the community. The project will benefit 140 migratory species, such as blue-winged teal, redhead, gadwall, green-winged teal, ring-necked duck, fulvous whistling-duck, piping plover, snowy plover, Wilson&apos;s plover, American oystercatcher, marbled godwit, black skimmer, least tern, and an important colony of reddish egret.</narrative>
  </description>
